# A constructor triggers an implied action that destroys a particle the action is blind to; the constructor resolves the destructor it knows through the action's Destruction Contract, reporting its unmet requirement.
define the potential action<my.domain.com:my_lib:/test> {
    it also assigns the action</callee>.
    it happens when {
        this particle is created.
    } and it does {
        define the position<box> {
            it may only contain particles where {
                it has the action</d>.
            }
        }
        create a particle in position<box>.
        move the particle in position<box> to action</callee>::position<incoming>.
    }
}
